node_modules
dist
dist-ssr
*.local
.DS_Store
.env
.env.*
# Anatomy assets are DOWNLOADED, not committed. The HRA whole-body models are
# 357 MB (female) and 230 MB (male); a single accidental `git add` of one would
# be effectively unrecoverable from history. docs/HRA_ASSETS.md has the URLs and
# public/models/README.md has the expected filenames, so the assets are always
# reproducible without storing them here.
public/models/*.glb
public/models/*.blend
public/models/*.gltf
public/models/*.bin
# ⚠️ AND ANY SUFFIXED VARIANT OF THOSE. `*.glb` does not match
# `bodyparts3d.ao.glb.prev`, which is the shape a hand-made backup takes when
# swapping a rebuilt asset in — and a `git add -A` during the 8 August rebuild
# duly staged 10.8 MB of it. Caught before it left the machine, but the comment
# above is explicit that one accidental add is effectively unrecoverable from
# history, so the pattern is widened rather than the habit trusted.
public/models/*.glb.*
public/models/*.gltf.*
# The ANNY bake's provenance manifest. It describes assets that are not
# committed, so committing it would leave a record of a build nobody has —
# and the parameters it records are already in `src/scene/bodyEnvelopes.ts`
# and `licences.json`, which ARE reviewed. `npm run bake:anny` rewrites it.
public/models/anny-provenance.json
# The phenotype grid's sidecar, likewise: it describes a 28 MB .bin that is not
# committed, and `npm run bake:anny-grid` rewrites both together.
public/models/anny-grid.json
# And the grid's topology. `*.bin` above does not match `.idx`, so without this
# line a `git add -A` commits 321 KB of binary that the same bake regenerates —
# the third time a generated asset has slipped past a pattern that looked
# exhaustive. All three grid files are written by one command; none is committed.
public/models/anny-grid.idx

# build info
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
.gstack/

# CT atlas pipeline (docs/CT_ATLAS_PIPELINE.md). The venv holds torch and the
# MOOSE weights, which land INSIDE the package directory
# (moosez/models/nnunet_trained_models/) at ~240 MB per model — about 2 GB for
# the eight whole-body CT models. Nothing here is source; it is all rebuildable
# from scripts/ct-atlas/requirements.txt plus one `run_moose.py` invocation.
scripts/ct-atlas/.venv/
# Segmentations and intermediate NIfTIs. These are DERIVED FROM PATIENT IMAGING
# and must never be committed even when small — see CLAUDE.md constraint 3.
scripts/ct-atlas/work/
*.nii
*.nii.gz

# Python bytecode from the CT-atlas tooling
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
scripts/ct-atlas/.venv/

# Third-party reference documents dropped in for reading. Not ours to
# redistribute — keep them local and cite them instead.
nako_verf.txt

# MOOSE/CT working cache — rebuildable, and large.
scripts/ct-atlas/.cache/

# OLS4 response cache for the FMA ↔ UBERON bridge. Pure derived data — every
# entry is re-fetchable from the EBI API, and committing it would freeze a
# snapshot of somebody else's ontology inside this repository.
.cache/
